
@startuml
title COLORS Web Application - Class Diagram

left to right direction
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

class "code.js" as Frontend <<JavaScript Module>> {
    - userId: int
    - firstName: string
    - lastName: string
    --
    + doLogin()
    + saveCookie()
    + readCookie()
    + doLogout()
    + addColor()
    + searchColor()
}

class "Login.php" as Login <<PHP Endpoint>> {
    + getRequestInfo()
    + returnWithInfo()
    + returnWithError()
}

class "AddColor.php" as AddColor <<PHP Endpoint>> {
    + getRequestInfo()
    + returnWithError()
}

class "SearchColors.php" as SearchColors <<PHP Endpoint>> {
    + getRequestInfo()
    + returnWithInfo()
    + returnWithError()
}

class "db.php" as Database <<PHP Module>> {
    + conn: mysqli
}

class "Users" as Users <<MySQL Table>> {
    + ID: int
    + FirstName: string
    + LastName: string
    + Login: string
    + Password: string
}

class "Colors" as Colors <<MySQL Table>> {
    + ID: int
    + Name: string
    + UserID: int
}

Frontend ..> Login : Login request
Frontend ..> AddColor : Add color request
Frontend ..> SearchColors : Search request

Login ..> Database : Uses connection
AddColor ..> Database : Uses connection
SearchColors ..> Database : Uses connection

Login ..> Users : Reads
AddColor ..> Colors : Inserts
SearchColors ..> Colors : Searches

Users "1" -- "0..*" Colors : owns

note bottom of Colors
  UserID links colors to users logically.
  The lab SQL does not declare a foreign key.
end note

note bottom of Frontend
  JavaScript and PHP use procedural functions.
  Module boxes represent files, not actual OOP classes.
end note

@enduml
